  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A boat moves due east at 8 km/h in still water while a current flows due north at 6 km/h. (a) Write the resultant velocity as a column vector. (b) Calculate the magnitude of the resultant velocity. (c) Write a unit vector in the direction of the resultant velocity."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: East is the positive x-direction and north is the positive y-direction, so the two speeds slot straight into a column vector."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p191_q18.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p191-q18 from workbook page 191."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Write the eastward speed as the x-component and the northward speed as the y-component.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "8 east, 6 north"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: v = (8, 6) km/h"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Apply Pythagoras to the two components.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "√(8² + 6²) = √(64 + 36) = √100"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: |v| = 10 km/h"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Divide each component of v by its magnitude.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(1/10)(8, 6)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: unit vector = (0.8, 0.6)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Place 8 as the x-component and 6 as the y-component, use Pythagoras for the magnitude, then divide the vector by that magnitude."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) Resultant velocity = (8, 6) km/h  (b) Magnitude = √(8² + 6²) = √100 = 10 km/h  (c) Unit vector = (1/10)(8, 6) = (0.8, 0.6)"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "East and north are perpendicular, so the two velocities form the legs of a right-angled triangle and the resultant is its hypotenuse. Dividing a vector by its own length keeps the direction but scales the length to exactly 1, which is what a unit vector means. Checking (0.8)² + (0.6)² = 1 confirms it."
    }
  ],
